Experiment 8: Develop a program to detect the gas leakage in the surrounding environment.

AIM: To develop and implement a program that detects the presence of gas leakage in the surrounding environment using sensor readings and generates an alert when the gas concentration exceeds a predefined safety threshold.

COMPONENTS:


Sl. No.	Quantity	Component
1	1	Arduino Uno R3
2	1	USB Cable
3	5	Jumper Wires
4	1	MQ-5 Gas Sensor
5	1	Buzzer

CIRCUIT DIAGRAM:

 


Gas Sensor	Arduino
A0	A0
GND	GND
VCC	5V

Buzzer	Arduino
+	D8
-	GND
 

SETUP:

a) Connect the MQ-5 Gas Sensor to the Arduino Uno as per the circuit diagram (A0 → A0, VCC → 5V, GND → GND).
b) Connect the Buzzer to the Arduino Uno (Positive → D8, Negative → GND). c) Connect the Arduino Uno to the computer using a USB cable.
d) Open the Arduino IDE, then go to Tools → Board and select Arduino Uno. e) In Tools → Port, select the COM port of the connected Arduino Uno.
f) Type the program into the Arduino IDE and upload it.
g) Open the Serial Monitor (baud rate 9600) to observe sensor readings and alerts when gas concentration exceeds the threshold.

CODE:

// Gas Sensor (MQ-5) with Buzzer Program

const int gasSensorPin = A0; // Analog pin for MQ-5 sensor const int buzzerPin = 8; // Digital pin for buzzer
const int threshold = 500; // Threshold for buzzer and alert void setup() {
pinMode(buzzerPin, OUTPUT); Serial.begin(9600);
}

void loop() {

int sensorValue = analogRead(gasSensorPin);

// Print sensor value Serial.print("Gas Sensor Value: "); Serial.println(sensorValue);
// If smoke value > 500 => Alert + buzzer ON

if (sensorValue > threshold) {

Serial.println("ALERT: Smoke detected! Buzzer ON!");

digitalWrite(buzzerPin, HIGH);

} else {
 

Serial.println("Safe: Smoke level normal.");

digitalWrite(buzzerPin, LOW);

} delay(200); RESULT:
The Arduino Uno successfully detected gas leakage using the MQ-5 sensor.

When the gas concentration was below the threshold (500), the Serial Monitor displayed
“Safe: Gas level normal.” and the buzzer remained OFF.

When the gas concentration exceeded the threshold, the Serial Monitor displayed “ALERT: Gas leakage detected! Buzzer ON!” and the buzzer turned ON, giving an audible warning.

Thus, the experiment was successfully implemented to detect gas leakage and generate an alert both through the Serial Monitor and a buzzer.
